摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"仿 Claude Code 推理等级滑块 支持第三方模型 DSH 插件","id":"gh:1335766616","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-effort-slider","slug":"2768651338/dsh-effort-slider","topics":["claude-code","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","effort-slider","webgl"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"仿 Claude Code 推理等级滑块 支持第三方模型 DSH 插件"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-effort-slider"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **A Claude Code–style reasoning-effort slider for DeepSeek Harness** — click **Effort** in the mod"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"el menu, drag without steps, snap on release, with a WebGL fire trail; any third-party model/provide"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"r gets real, working thinking-effort control."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**English** · 中文 · Español · 日本語 · Deutsch · Русский · Português · 한국어"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Click the **Effort** row (second row of the official model menu) instead of the built-in level list:"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" an **Effort slider panel** pops up — OFF/MAX scale ticks, Low/Medium/High/Ultracode status shown li"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ve, and after the panel closes the effort value stays color-coded on the menu row and on the model-s"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"anel closes the effort value stays color-coded on the menu row and on the model-seat trigger button."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Features · Compatibility · Install / Uninstall · Quick Start · Configuration · Permissions & Data · "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"How It Works · Troubleshooting · Development"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Demo screenshots** (menu-row coloring / model-seat trigger / Effort panel — effort level is color-"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"screenshots** (menu-row coloring / model-seat trigger / Effort panel — effort level is color-coded):"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Menu row | Model-seat trigger | Effort panel |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> 🔧 **v0.5.2** — Update the DSH development baseline to **0.2.1-rc.5** and validate packed releases "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"on **rc.4 / rc.5**. Fix the stale npm 0.5.1 client artifact that still registered `dsh-effort-slider"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"`, causing duplicate factory registration and a desktop startup reload loop. Packing now rebuilds th"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"e client and checks the actual JavaScript registration against the manifest, so a stale unscoped bun"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"dle cannot ship again. Mouse dragging now survives catalog refreshes triggered by live effort writes"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"; requests are serialized with only the latest pending level retained, and the current model is chec"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ked again before saving.\n>\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Feature | Description |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| 🎚️ Stepless dragging | Continuous 0–100 dragging that writes `reasoningEffort` in real time (16 ms"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" throttle, no request pile-up while dragging) |\n| 🎯 Snap on release | Snaps to the nearest level on "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"release / blur / keyboard end, with one confirmation write |\n| 🔥 WebGL fire trail | Three-pass shade"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"rs (ignite → blur → composite); the fire front follows the thumb with spring damping |\n| 🏁 OFF/MAX t"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"icks | First/last levels always show `OFF` / `MAX`; middle levels show the API-returned name |\n| 🎨 L"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"evel status | Effort name shown in the panel header, colored/glowing per level; menu row and model-s"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"eat trigger keep the same color after closing (v0.2.3) |\n| 🌐 Universal effort | Third-party models w"},{"id":"p12s8","text":"ithout `reasoning` metadata automatically get the universal 5-level scale; pi-ai models get wire-lev"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"el dictionaries patched in, **hot-applied** (v0.2.0) |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Only `reasoningEffort` is written — model selection is untouched. Models with no multi-level reasoni"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ng show 「当前模型不提供多档推理等级」 (no multi-level reasoning available)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Universal effort provisioning (v0.2.0, simplified in v0.3.0)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**Any custom third-party model/provider gets thinking-effort control that actually works on the wire"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ny custom third-party model/provider gets thinking-effort control that actually works on the wire**:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **Wire-level provisioning (host, pi-ai)**: for `llm-pi-ai` models missing `reasoningEfforts`, the "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"dictionary and `compat` wire dialect\nare patched in (**hot-applied, no restart**); pi-ai translates "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"the level into real wire fields\n(`reasoning_effort` / `thinking` / OpenRouter `reasoning.effort`, et"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"c.) **and** advertises the same declaration as the model's\n`reasoning` catalog metadata — which is w"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"hat makes the official **Effort** row appear for a hand-declared model at all;\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Item | Value |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| DSH version | **0.2.1-rc.4 / 0.2.1-rc.5**; development types pinned to rc.5, real web profiles on "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"Windows |\n| Broken on | DSH ≤ 0.1.5 — v0.4.0 targets the `SettingsForms` settings service introduced"},{"id":"p19s3","text":" in 0.2.0 (use v0.3.0 for DSH 0.1.5; v0.2.5 and earlier also import `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"`, which was removed after 0.1.1-rc.2) |\n| Install mechanism | `dsh plugin --profile web add` (bundl"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"e patch + dual half) |\n| Depends on | `ctx.sessions` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller`) and"},{"id":"p19s6","text":" `ctx.modelDirectories` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-model-selection`); host: `ctx.llm`, `ctx.settin"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"gs` (`SettingsForms`) |\n| Client module requests | none beyond the platform baseline (`react`, `reac"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"t-dom/client`, `react/jsx-runtime`) — all DSH imports are type-only and erased |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## How It Works"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Half | File | Role |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Host | `lib/index.js` | Universal effort provisioning: locates the pi-ai profile entry (`llm-pi-ai"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"`), reads it via `settings.describe()`, patches wire dialects (`buildProvisionOps`, idempotent, resp"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ects user declarations) via `settings.mutate`; listens to `llm/adapters-updated` / `settings/documen"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"t-updated`. With `debugReport: true`, each provisioning run logs a per-route/per-model report (writt"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"en fields or skip reason, plus a note where the wire dialect does not apply) instead of the one-line"},{"id":"p22s6","text":" count, and each model call is traced as `[debug] request route=… model=… effort=…` through a read-o"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"nly `llm/stream` passthrough |\n| Browser | `lib/client.js` | Captures clicks on the model menu's Eff"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"ort row → shows the Effort panel; reads `ctx.modelDirectories.directoryFor(sessionId)` and writes th"},{"id":"p22s9","text":"rough `directory.select({ reasoningEffort })`; a MutationObserver keeps the menu-row level color ali"},{"id":"p22s10","text":"ve after the panel closes |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> The browser half follows the official external-plugin convention: classic script + `window.__Modul"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"eLoader__.load` factory;\n> `react` / `react-dom/client` / `react/jsx-runtime` are platform externals"},{"id":"p23s3","text":";\n> `effort.module.css` is hashed and inlined by lightningcss, injected as `<style data-plugin>` whe"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"css` is hashed and inlined by lightningcss, injected as `<style data-plugin>` when the factory runs."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## License & Security"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"**License**: BSD-3-Clause — see LICENSE.\nThe UI implementation references the aurora skin of the com"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"munity dsh-ui-web project (BSD-3-Clause); full upstream notices and license texts are in\nTHIRD_PARTY"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"i-web project (BSD-3-Clause); full upstream notices and license texts are in\nTHIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"**Security**: this plugin reads no credentials and sends nothing over the network (only talks to the"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" local DSH). To report a security issue privately, use GitHub's **Report a vulnerability** on the Se"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"curity tab — do not open a public issue with exploit details."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
